{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}About S2S — Why we are rebuilding the menu workflow{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Learn why S2S combines permanent QR links, structured menu management, and owner-reviewed AI to modernize how venues publish information.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <section class="about-hero">
        <div class="shell about-hero-grid">
            <div class="about-hero-copy" data-reveal>
                <span class="eyebrow">About Scan to See</span>
                <h1>A menu should evolve without making its QR code obsolete.</h1>
                <p>S2S is built around a simple operational truth: prices, availability, services, and customer expectations change constantly. Printed links should not.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-manifesto" data-reveal>
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">format_quote</span>
                <blockquote>Keep the physical entry point permanent. Make everything behind it easy to improve.</blockquote>
                <p>The product principle behind every S2S workflow</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-facts">
        <div class="shell fact-row" data-reveal>
            <div><strong>1</strong><span>permanent public QR per menu</span></div>
            <div><strong>0</strong><span>apps required for customers</span></div>
            <div><strong>100%</strong><span>owner review before AI data is saved</span></div>
            <div><strong>2</strong><span>ways to start: build or scan</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story">
        <div class="shell story-grid">
            <div class="sticky-heading" data-reveal>
                <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
                <h2>Most menu tools solve only the last ten seconds.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="story-content">
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="story-index">01</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>A QR code alone does not create a maintainable menu.</h3>
                        <p>Venues still need to structure categories, retype items, manage prices, prepare translations, and keep availability accurate. S2S treats the QR as the entry point to a complete content workflow.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="story-index">02</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Existing paper should not be discarded as a starting point.</h3>
                        <p>Many businesses already have a handwritten or printed menu. The AI Scanner beta turns that document into a proposed structure, reducing repetitive setup while keeping the owner responsible for validation.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="story-index">03</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Subscription changes should not destroy business data.</h3>
                        <p>S2S separates public availability from data ownership. If access pauses, the menu structure and publication choices remain preserved so the same experience can return after renewal.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-principles">
        <div class="shell">
            <div class="section-split-head" data-reveal>
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">What guides the product</span>
                    <h2>Four principles behind the platform.</h2>
                </div>
                <p>They shape the data model, the owner experience, and what customers see after a scan.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principles-grid">
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">link</span>
                    <h3>Stable links</h3>
                    <p>The menu slug remains stable while content, presentation, and availability change freely.</p>
                </article>
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">visibility</span>
                    <h3>Human oversight</h3>
                    <p>AI proposes a draft. The owner reviews and corrects it before the application saves menu content.</p>
                </article>
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">shield</span>
                    <h3>Non-destructive controls</h3>
                    <p>Plan enforcement archives overflow safely instead of deleting menu data without recovery.</p>
                </article>
                <article data-reveal>
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">phone_iphone</span>
                    <h3>Guest simplicity</h3>
                    <p>Customer pages prioritize fast mobile access with no login, account, or installation step.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-system">
        <div class="shell system-grid">
            <div data-reveal>
                <span class="eyebrow">One connected system</span>
                <h2>Different users, one reliable source of truth.</h2>
                <p>The owner workspace, AI pipeline, subscription controls, and public menu all work from the same structured data rather than disconnected copies.</p>
                <a class="text-link" href="{{ path('app_ai_scanner') }}">Explore the AI workflow <span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="system-map" data-reveal>
                <div class="system-node">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">storefront</span>
                    <strong>Owner</strong><small>Creates and approves</small>
                </div>
                <span class="system-arrow material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span>
                <div class="system-node is-accent">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">database</span>
                    <strong>S2S menu</strong><small>Structured source</small>
                </div>
                <span class="system-arrow material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span>
                <div class="system-node">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">qr_code_scanner</span>
                    <strong>Customer</strong><small>Scans and browses</small>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="s-cta s-cta--new">
        <div class="shell cta-panel" data-reveal>
            <div>
                <span class="eyebrow">Build with us</span>
                <h2>Turn your current menu into a digital experience that can keep improving.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-actions">
                <a class="btn btn-primary btn-icon" href="{{ path('app_register') }}">Create an account <span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span></a>
                <a class="cta-secondary-link" href="{{ path('app_pricing') }}">View pricing</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
